/**
 * swe.ch8.l5 — "Chapter 8 Review and Project: The Mini-Git Model /
 * مراجعة الفصل 8 ومشروع: نموذج Git المصغّر"
 * Aligned with SWE ch8 s8 (8.8 Conclusion, p.222) — chapter recap + closing project.
 * All expression is original (own-words paraphrase of the CC BY-SA 4.0 source).
 * SIMULATED-GIT PATTERN (kept from l1–l4): git itself appears only in display-only
 * prose; every runnable field is a pure-Python DAG model — commits as snapshot
 * dicts {'id','parent','msg','files'} linked by parent, branches as dict
 * name->commit-id pointers, merge() fast-forwarding or reporting the first
 * conflicting file from snapshot diffs against the merge base. Deterministic,
 * no randomness, no input(), no git execution claims.
 */
