    },
    {
      kind: 'exercise',
      id: 'ex2.project-minigit',
      exKind: 'write_code',
      required: true,
      prompt: {
        ar: "المشروع: نموذج Git المصغّر. 1) عرّف صنف MiniGit بحالة: self.commits قاموس id->التزام، وself.branches قاموس اسم->التزام يبدأ بـ {'main': None}، وself.head اسم الفرع النشط يبدأ 'main'، وself.files قاموس ملف->نسخة، وself.next_id عدّاد يبدأ 1. 2) التوابع: change(self, fname, version) يسجّل نسخة ملف في شجرة العمل؛ commit(self, msg) يبني التزام {'id': cid, 'parent': self.branches[self.head], 'msg': msg, 'files': dict(self.files)} بمعرّف 'c%d' من العدّاد ثم يحرّك مؤشر الفرع الحالي إليه ويعيد المعرف — لاحظ أن كل التزام يحمل لقطة كاملة للملفات (commits-as-snapshots)؛ branch(self, name) ينسخ مؤشر الفرع الحالي إلى اسم جديد؛ checkout(self, name) يبدّل self.head ويستعيد شجرة العمل من لقطة طرف ذلك الفرع: self.files = dict(self.commits[tip]['files']) متى كان للفرع طرف — كما يفعل git checkout على جهازك حين يبدّل محتوى المجلد؛ merge(self, source) يفحص أولًا fast-forward (إن كان طرفنا سلفًا لطرف المصدر فحرّك مؤشرنا وحدّث الملفات من لقطة المصدر وأعِد 'fast-forward')، وإلا امشِ من طرفنا إلى الجذور واعثر على أول سلف مشترك، وقارن لقطتَي الطرفين مع لقطة الأصل: أي ملف غيّره الطرفان معًا يعيد 'conflict: <file>' (أول اسم مرتبًا)، وإلا طبّق تغييرات المصدر وأعِد 'merged'، وإن كان الطرفان متساويين أعِد 'already up to date'. 3) السائق: التزامان على main (app.py ثم config.py)، فرع dev وانتقل إليه والتزامان (search.py ثم config.py بنسخة أخرى)، عُد إلى main والتزام ثالث يغيّر config.py أيضًا، ثم اطبع 'commits: %d' مع len(mg.commits) و'branches: %d' مع len(mg.branches) ونتيجة merge('dev'). المتوقع: commits: 5 ثم branches: 2 ثم conflict: config.py.",
        en: "The project: the Mini-Git Model. 1) Define a class MiniGit with state: self.commits a dict id->commit, self.branches a dict name->commit starting as {'main': None}, self.head the active branch name starting 'main', self.files a dict file->version, and self.next_id a counter starting at 1. 2) Methods: change(self, fname, version) records a file version in the working tree; commit(self, msg) builds {'id': cid, 'parent': self.branches[self.head], 'msg': msg, 'files': dict(self.files)} with a 'c%d' id from the counter, then moves the current branch pointer to it and returns the id — note every commit carries a full snapshot of the files (commits-as-snapshots); branch(self, name) copies the current branch pointer to a new name; checkout(self, name) switches self.head and restores the working tree from that branch\u2019s tip snapshot: self.files = dict(self.commits[tip]['files']) whenever the branch has a tip — exactly what git checkout does on your own machine when it swaps the folder\u2019s contents; merge(self, source) first checks fast-forward (if our tip is an ancestor of the source tip, move our pointer, update files from the source snapshot, return 'fast-forward'); otherwise walk from our tip to the roots to find the first common ancestor, compare both sides\u2019 snapshots against the ancestor\u2019s: any file both sides changed returns 'conflict: <file>' (first sorted name); otherwise apply the source-side changes and return 'merged'; when both tips are equal return 'already up to date'. 3) Driver: two commits on main (app.py then config.py), a dev branch you check out with two commits (search.py then config.py with another version), back to main for a third commit touching config.py too, then print 'commits: %d' with len(mg.commits), 'branches: %d' with len(mg.branches), and the result of merge('dev'). Expected: commits: 5, then branches: 2, then conflict: config.py.",
      },
      starterCode: "class MiniGit:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.commits = {}\n        self.branches = {'main': None}\n        self.head = 'main'\n        self.files = {}\n        self.next_id = 1\n\n    def change(self, fname, version):\n        # سجّل نسخة الملف في شجرة العمل / record the file version in the working tree\n        pass\n\n    def commit(self, msg):\n        # ابنِ التزام باللقطة ثم حرّك مؤشر الفرع الحالي / build the commit with its snapshot, then move the branch pointer\n        pass\n\n    def branch(self, name):\n        # انسخ مؤشر الفرع الحالي إلى اسم جديد / copy the current pointer to a new name\n        pass\n\n    def checkout(self, name):\n        # بدّل الفرع ثم استعد شجرة العمل من لقطة الطرف / switch the branch, then restore the working tree from the tip snapshot\n        pass\n\n\nmg = MiniGit()\nmg.change('app.py', 'v1')\nmg.commit('Add app skeleton')\nmg.change('config.py', 'base')\nmg.commit('Add shared config')\nmg.branch('dev')\nmg.checkout('dev')\nmg.change('search.py', 'dev-v1')\nmg.commit('Add search box')\nmg.change('config.py', 'dev-v2')\nmg.commit('Tune config for search')\nmg.checkout('main')\nmg.change('config.py', 'main-v2')\nmg.commit('Tune config for pages')\nprint('commits: %d' % len(mg.commits))\nprint('branches: %d' % len(mg.branches))\nprint(mg.merge('dev'))",
      solution: "class MiniGit:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.commits = {}\n        self.branches = {'main': None}\n        self.head = 'main'\n        self.files = {}\n        self.next_id = 1\n\n    def change(self, fname, version):\n        self.files[fname] = version\n\n    def commit(self, msg):\n        cid = 'c%d' % self.next_id\n        self.next_id = self.next_id + 1\n        self.commits[cid] = {'id': cid, 'parent': self.branches[self.head], 'msg': msg, 'files': dict(self.files)}\n        self.branches[self.head] = cid\n        return cid\n\n    def branch(self, name):\n        self.branches[name] = self.branches[self.head]\n\n    def checkout(self, name):\n        self.head = name\n        tip = self.branches[name]\n        if tip is not None:\n            self.files = dict(self.commits[tip]['files'])\n\n    def merge(self, source):\n        ours = self.branches[self.head]\n        theirs = self.branches[source]\n        if ours == theirs:\n            return 'already up to date'\n        node = theirs\n        while node is not None:\n            if node == ours:\n                self.branches[self.head] = theirs\n                self.files = dict(self.commits[theirs]['files'])\n                return 'fast-forward'\n            node = self.commits[node]['parent']\n\n        def ancestors(tip):\n            chain = []\n            node = tip\n            while node is not None:\n                chain.append(node)\n                node = self.commits[node]['parent']\n            return chain\n\n        base = None\n        for cid in ancestors(ours):\n            if cid in ancestors(theirs):\n                base = cid\n                break\n        base_files = self.commits[base]['files']\n        ours_files = self.commits[ours]['files']\n        theirs_files = self.commits[theirs]['files']\n        ours_changed = set()\n        for fname, ver in ours_files.items():\n            if base_files.get(fname) != ver:\n                ours_changed.add(fname)\n        theirs_changed = set()\n        for fname, ver in theirs_files.items():\n            if base_files.get(fname) != ver:\n                theirs_changed.add(fname)\n        conflicts = sorted(ours_changed & theirs_changed)\n        if conflicts:\n            return 'conflict: %s' % conflicts[0]\n        for fname, ver in theirs_files.items():\n            if base_files.get(fname) != ver:\n                self.files[fname] = ver\n        return 'merged'\n\n\nmg = MiniGit()\nmg.change('app.py', 'v1')\nmg.commit('Add app skeleton')\nmg.change('config.py', 'base')\nmg.commit('Add shared config')\nmg.branch('dev')\nmg.checkout('dev')\nmg.change('search.py', 'dev-v1')\nmg.commit('Add search box')\nmg.change('config.py', 'dev-v2')\nmg.commit('Tune config for search')\nmg.checkout('main')\nmg.change('config.py', 'main-v2')\nmg.commit('Tune config for pages')\nprint('commits: %d' % len(mg.commits))\nprint('branches: %d' % len(mg.branches))\nprint(mg.merge('dev'))",
      tests: [
