      kind: 'debug',
      id: 'ex5.debug-stale-pointer',
      required: true,
      brokenCode: "class MiniGit:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.commits = {}\n        self.branches = {'main': None}\n        self.head = 'main'\n        self.next_id = 1\n\n    def commit(self, msg):\n        cid = 'c%d' % self.next_id\n        self.next_id = self.next_id + 1\n        self.commits[cid] = {'id': cid, 'parent': self.branches[self.head], 'msg': msg}\n        # الخلل هنا: سجل التزامًا ونسي شيئًا / THE FLAW: recorded a commit and forgot something\n        return cid\n\n    def log(self):\n        lines = []\n        node = self.branches[self.head]\n        while node is not None:\n            lines.append('%s %s' % (node, self.commits[node]['msg']))\n            node = self.commits[node]['parent']\n        return lines\n\n\ng = MiniGit()\ng.commit('Add app skeleton')\ng.commit('Add search box')\nprint('commits: %d' % len(g.commits))\nfor line in g.log():\n    print(line)",
      prompt: {
        ar: 'شغّل الكود المعطوب ولاحظ الفضيحة: التزامان موجودان في commits — ومع ذلك لا يطبع السجل شيئًا على الإطلاق! لا استثناء ولا انهيار: التاريخ يبدو فارغًا رغم وجود الالتزامات. اسأل نفسك: من أين يبدأ log مشيه؟ من self.branches[self.head] — ولم يتحرك هذا المؤشر أبدًا بعد أول التزام، فبقي None وكل التزام جديد وُلد أبوه None بلا رابط بالسابق. أصلح الخلل بإضافة السطر الناقص في commit بعد بناء التزام: self.branches[self.head] = cid — المؤشر يتحرك مع كل التزام، فيصير السجل حيًّا: c2 ثم c1.',
        en: 'Run the broken code and witness the scandal: two commits exist in commits — yet the log prints nothing at all! No exception, no crash: history looks empty though the commits are there. Ask yourself: where does log start its walk? From self.branches[self.head] — and that pointer never moved after the first commit, so it stayed None and every new commit was born with None as its parent, disconnected from the past. Fix the flaw by adding the missing line in commit after building the commit: self.branches[self.head] = cid — the pointer moves with every commit, and the log comes alive: c2 then c1.',
      },
      solution: "class MiniGit:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.commits = {}\n        self.branches = {'main': None}\n        self.head = 'main'\n        self.next_id = 1\n\n    def commit(self, msg):\n        cid = 'c%d' % self.next_id\n        self.next_id = self.next_id + 1\n        self.commits[cid] = {'id': cid, 'parent': self.branches[self.head], 'msg': msg}\n        self.branches[self.head] = cid\n        return cid\n\n    def log(self):\n        lines = []\n        node = self.branches[self.head]\n        while node is not None:\n            lines.append('%s %s' % (node, self.commits[node]['msg']))\n            node = self.commits[node]['parent']\n        return lines\n\n\ng = MiniGit()\ng.commit('Add app skeleton')\ng.commit('Add search box')\nprint('commits: %d' % len(g.commits))\nfor line in g.log():\n    print(line)",
      tests: [
